        "model": "sonar-pro",
        "messages": {
          "message": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "You are the sole research stage for an article. Perform one bounded research pass.\n\n- Prioritise primary sources, official documentation, papers, filings and direct reports.\n- Cross-check consequential claims against at least two independent sources where possible.\n- Separate verified fact from interpretation.\n- Surface uncertainty, disagreement, incentives and practical trade-offs.\n- Prefer current information, but include foundational older sources where needed.\n- Return a concise structured brief with inline source URLs and a final Sources section.\n- Do not write the article."
            },
            {
              "role": "user",
              "content": "={{ $json.output || $json.mainPrompt || '' }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "simplify": true,
        "options": {
          "maxTokens": 5000,
          "temperature": 0.2,
          "searchMode": "web",
          "webSearchOptions": "{\"search_context_size\":\"medium\"}"
        }
      },
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 2000
    },
    {
      "id": "article",
      "name": "Article Agent",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        -440,
        520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "={{ $json.message }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are Roman Travnikov's long-form blog editor.\n\nORIGINAL BRIEF\n{{ $('Brief Agent').item.json.output }}\n\nRESEARCH\n{{ $json.message }}\n\nCITATIONS RETURNED BY RESEARCH\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.citations || []) }}\n\nWrite the canonical English article. Social posts are derived from it later, so it must stand on its own.\n\nVOICE\n- Clear, conversational, direct, technically literate, sceptical of hype.\n- Explain complex terms simply without talking down.\n- Prefer production lessons and honest trade-offs.\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n- 900-1,600 words unless the topic genuinely needs less.\n- One clear thesis, descriptive H2 sections, short paragraphs, a decisive conclusion.\n- Use only evidence from the research. Never invent facts or citations.\n- Mark uncertainty plainly where evidence is contested.\n- No corporate filler, no fake personal anecdotes, no generic AI phrasing.\n- Regular hyphens, never em dashes.\n- If the piece is seasonal or tied to a year, state the target year explicitly in the title and the first sentence, and label prior-year figures as baseline.\n\nReturn exactly one valid JSON object, no code fence:\n{\n  \"title\": \"...\",\n  \"slug\": \"lowercase-kebab-case\",\n  \"excerpt\": \"one concise paragraph\",\n  \"body\": \"complete Markdown article, without repeating the title\",\n  \"tags\": [\"three\", \"lowercase\", \"tags\"],\n  \"seoTitle\": \"under 60 characters\",\n  \"seoDescription\": \"under 160 characters\",\n  \"citations\": [\"https://...\"]\n}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "model-Model (Article)",
